course: dictionary
lesson: 2978
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Dubbing is one of these words. «Dubbing means recording new voices in another language» is about films and shows, where new actors speak in a different language.
explain: Dubbing can also mean giving someone a nickname, or the old ceremony of making someone a knight. Look at the clues. A film, a screen or a new voice points to the first meaning. A castle, a sword or a king points to the knight meaning. Boots and leather point to the old grease.
explain: Use the swap test to check. Put your meaning in place of the word and see if the sentence still makes sense. «The dubbing is bad» means the new voices are poor, not that a nickname or a knight is poor. If your meaning does not fit, try another one.
fact: Dubbing is a word with four meanings, so check the context before you choose one.
fact: «Dubbing» (film) means replacing the spoken words of a film or show with words in another language, said by new voice actors.
fact: «Dubbing» (nickname) means giving someone or something a nickname.
fact: «Dubbing» (history) means the ceremony of making someone a knight.
fact: «Dubbing» (old) also means «dubbin», a grease that makes leather boots soft and waterproof.
exercise: «Dubbing means recording new voices in another language.» What does dubbing mean in a film? | *Replacing the spoken words with words in another language | Giving someone a nickname | Making someone a knight | Rubbing grease into boots
exercise: Some countries prefer subtitles, the written words at the bottom of the screen. What are subtitles? | Spoken words said by new voice actors | A grease for leather boots | A nickname for a film | *The written words at the bottom of the screen
exercise: Her friends started dubbing her Speedy after sports day. What does dubbing mean here? | Recording new voices for a film | Making her boots waterproof | *Giving her a nickname | Making her a knight
test: In history, dubbing was the ceremony that made a man a knight. What does dubbing mean in this sentence? | A nickname for a soldier | A type of leather grease | *A ceremony of making someone a knight | A film with new voices
test: Which meaning of dubbing is about leather? | Replacing voices in a film | Making a knight | Giving a nickname | *A grease that makes boots soft and waterproof
exam: Alia reads «The dubbing is bad» in a film review. Which meaning fits best? | The boots are poor | *The new voices in the film are poor | The knight is poor | The nickname is poor
